        {
          "title": "3. Energy Is Never Lost",
          "sequenceOrder": 3,
          "status": "published",
          "xpReward": 55,
          "maxReattempts": 3,
          "passingThreshold": 60,
          "estimatedDuration": 9,
          "difficulty": "MEDIUM",
          "learnBlocks": [
            {
              "id": "p68-6-1",
              "type": "blob_dialog",
              "content": "One last idea, and it is the biggest one in physics.",
              "metadata": {
                "version": 1,
                "lines": [
                  {
                    "id": "l1",
                    "text": "One last idea, and it is the biggest one in physics.",
                    "mood": "thinking",
                    "cta": "Go on"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "l2",
                    "text": "Add up all the energy before a change and after it. The totals match. Every time.",
                    "mood": "surprised",
                    "cta": "Every time?"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "l3",
                    "text": "Every time. That rule is called conservation of energy.",
                    "mood": "cheer",
                    "cta": "Gotcha"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "p68-6-2",
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A ball dropped from your hand: **stored** height energy becomes **movement**, then **sound and heat** when it lands. Nothing vanishes, it only spreads out."
            },
            {
              "id": "p68-6-3",
              "type": "callout",
              "content": "This is why a bouncing ball never returns to the height it was dropped from. Some energy left as sound and heat on the first bounce."
            }
          ],
          "evaluateBlocks": [
            {
              "id": "p68-eb-6-1",
              "type": "order_steps",
              "question": "Follow the energy of a dropped ball, in order.",
              "correctAnswer": "stored>moving>bang",
              "explanation": "Height energy becomes movement on the way down, and the landing turns that into sound and heat.",
              "metadata": {
                "version": 1,
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "id": "stored",
                    "label": "Stored energy while you hold it up"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "moving",
                    "label": "Movement energy as it falls"
                  },
